Subject: [PATCH] fire OrderDriverAssigned event when PUT /v1/orders/{id} changes driver

The public OrderController::update() already wires the `driver` request field
through to `driver_assigned_uuid`, but it saves via `$order->update($input)`,
which skips the side-effect path that Order::assignDriver() takes — most
importantly the `OrderDriverAssigned` event that drives the
`order.driver_assigned` webhook downstream. As a result KromeOS (and any other
webhook consumer) never receives a driver-assigned event for reassignments
performed via the public API.

Calling `$order->assignDriver()` directly would double-save the model (once
inside assignDriver, once at the existing `$order->update($input)`). Instead
we capture the before/after driver_assigned_uuid, let the existing single
update() save run, and fire `notifyDriverAssigned()` once on an actual delta.

Companion to KromeOS 4b (dispatcher drag-card-to-driver) — that feature needs
the upstream event to propagate; without this patch the webhook never fires
and KromeOS' local state machine stays stuck on the previous assignment.

Idempotent: the change-detection (`!==` compare against the existing column
value) means re-assigning the same driver fires nothing, so retries / replays
don't generate phantom events. Verified live against the KromeFleet container
with a registered webhook endpoint — first assign → SendResourceLifecycleWebhook
job enqueued for `order.driver_assigned`; re-assigning same driver → only the
routine LogApiRequest enqueues, no webhook job.

--- a/server/src/Http/Controllers/Api/v1/OrderController.php
+++ b/server/src/Http/Controllers/Api/v1/OrderController.php
@@ -362,11 +362,17 @@
         }

         // driver assignment
+        // Track whether the assignment actually changes so we can fire
+        // OrderDriverAssigned once after the single update() save below — calling
+        // $order->assignDriver() here would double-save the model.
+        $driverAssignmentChanged = false;
         if ($request->has('driver')) {
-            $input['driver_assigned_uuid'] = Utils::getUuid('drivers', [
+            $resolvedDriverUuid = Utils::getUuid('drivers', [
                 'public_id'    => $request->input('driver'),
                 'company_uuid' => session('company'),
             ]);
+            $driverAssignmentChanged = $order->driver_assigned_uuid !== $resolvedDriverUuid;
+            $input['driver_assigned_uuid'] = $resolvedDriverUuid;
         }

         // facilitator assignment
@@ -410,6 +416,14 @@
         $order->update($input);
         $order->flushAttributesCache();

+        // Fire OrderDriverAssigned so downstream consumers (KromeOS webhook bridge)
+        // get notified — $order->update($input) saves the column but skips the
+        // assignDriver() side-effect path. Only fire on an actual change so a
+        // no-op re-assignment doesn't generate noise events.
+        if ($driverAssignmentChanged) {
+            $order->notifyDriverAssigned();
+        }
+
         // response the order resource
         return new OrderResource($order);
     }
